{
  "id": "27890_shitekisuru",
  "headword": "指摘する",
  "reading": "してきする",
  "romaji": "shitekisuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to point out; to indicate; to identify",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to point out; to indicate; to identify (a problem, error)",
      "explanation": "To draw attention to a specific point — typically a mistake, problem, or noteworthy fact — by explicitly naming it. Common in discussion, criticism, and analysis."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27890_shitekisuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{誤|あやま}りを{指摘|してき}する。",
      "english": "To point out a mistake.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27890_shitekisuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{先生|せんせい}に{問題点|もんだいてん}を{指摘|してき}された。",
      "english": "The teacher pointed out the problems to me.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27890_shitekisuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{専門家|せんもんか}は、この{制度|せいど}には{欠陥|けっかん}があると{指摘|してき}している。",
      "english": "Experts point out that this system has flaws.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし}); what is pointed out is marked with を.\n- Pattern: [point]を{指摘|してき}する; ～と{指摘|してき}する (to point out that ～)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {誤|あやま}りを{指摘|してき}する: to point out an error\n- {問題点|もんだいてん}を{指摘|してき}する: to point out problems\n- {的確|てきかく}に{指摘|してき}する: to point out precisely\n\nNOTE: {指摘|してき} carries a critical or corrective nuance — it usually flags something wrong or in need of attention, unlike the neutral {示|しめ}す (to show, to indicate).",
